    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm seeing a lot of irregular dark spotting on some of the sherds, almost like they were patchy during the firing process rather than a uniform color change. Is that usually a sign of inconsistent kiln temperature, or could it be something related to the impurities in the local clay source?",
      "source": "evaluator"
