    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'll try to look closer at the organic content. One weird thing though, the way these shards are distributed in the trench is really chaotic. It's not just a neat layer; pieces are scattered all over the floor, and some seem out of place compared to the surrounding strata. Does that kind of sudden, messy fragmentation usually suggest a single catastrophic event, or is it more likely just post-depositional disturbance?",
