      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Chaotic, scattered fragmentation across a strata floor is often indicative of post-depositional disturbance rather than a single, instantaneous catastrophic event. Processes like bioturbation (animal activity), root intrusion, or even modern excavation activity can cause this mixing and scattering of artifacts. If the scattering pattern is highly stratified and seems concentrated in one area, a physical event might be possible, but general admixture usually suggests chronological mixing after burial.",
